#- Assertions
#-
#- "assert" checks a condition and names it. It only runs under "aurora test":
#- a plain "aurora run" warns about each one and carries on, so a program that
#- happens to hold an assertion does not fail because of it.
#-
#- This file tests greeting.ar — a test belongs to the source file of the same
#- name. That file is evaluated first, so hello, twice and bigger_of are in
#- scope here without being imported.
#-
#- Two things follow from that:
#-   - whatever the source does at its top level happens too (greeting.ar
#-     prints, so you will see its output during the test)
#-   - the two files share one scope, so declaring a name that greeting.ar
#-     already declares is a conflict, not a shadow
#-
#- Run: aurora test examples/greeting.test.ar
#-
#- Output:
#-   examples/greeting.test.ar
#-     ok    hello answers 1
#-     ok    twice doubles
#-     ok    twice of zero is zero
#-     ok    bigger_of takes the larger one
#-     ok    bigger_of is not fooled by order
#-
#-   5 passed, 0 failed in 1 file

assert(hello() equals 1, "hello answers 1");

assert(twice(21) equals 42, "twice doubles");
assert(twice(0) equals 0, "twice of zero is zero");

assert(bigger_of(10, 3) equals 10, "bigger_of takes the larger one");
assert(bigger_of(3, 10) equals 10, "bigger_of is not fooled by order");
